The central lesson is that identity, device integrity, cryptographic evidence and resource-level policy must work together. Zero Trust is therefore not a single product; it is an architectural approach spanning identity, endpoints, applications, data, networks and operational policy. NIST's newer SP 1800-35 implementation guidance demonstrates this broader approach through practical Zero Trust implementations, including identity, access control, microsegmentation and software-defined perimeter technologies. NIST Computer Security Resource Center
